<http://data.silknow.org/object/d6033f36-8194-3f29-a763-df63577584c9>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Scarf of woven silk and wool. Woven with a plain twill centre in white silk, and with deep borders of decoration at each end and narrow borders at the sides. The borders are woven separately and joined onto the ground. The side borders are 1.5 inch wide and contain flowers in pink or yellow outlined in red with touches of other colours. These flowers are linked by brown stems and leaves. Similar borders form the upper and lower edges of the decorative panels at each end. These end borders are 18 inches deep. They contain bunches of flowers tied with blue ribbons and linked by yellow stems forming cartouches. Much of the white ground is visible.\n\nThe centre is woven in silk in 2/1 twill. The side borders are woven chiefly in silk. The wefts are bound in 3/1 twill. The end panels are woven with a silk ground and most of the brocaded wefts are also silk. The ground is woven in 1/2 twill."@en , "Scarf of woven silk and wool, Great Britain, ca. 1825-1845"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/96bcd059-5d63-3c52-9607-7e58a9f25d85> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/683afd7b-04e8-39bb-b70d-00444c4133dd> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/066f0549-46a4-3b62-b9e4-147ec305a78a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/096c2734-3f69-35f1-b578-adb956329c3a> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Scarf of woven silk and wool. Woven with a plain twill centre in white silk, and with deep borders of decoration at each end and narrow borders at the sides. The borders are woven separately and joined onto the ground. The side borders are 1.5 inch wide and contain flowers in pink or yellow outlined in red with touches of other colours. These flowers are linked by brown stems and leaves. Similar borders form the upper and lower edges of the decorative panels at each end. These end borders are 18 inches deep. They contain bunches of flowers tied with blue ribbons and linked by yellow stems forming cartouches. Much of the white ground is visible.\n\nThe centre is woven in silk in 2/1 twill. The side borders are woven chiefly in silk. The wefts are bound in 3/1 twill. The end panels are woven with a silk ground and most of the brocaded wefts are also silk. The ground is woven in 1/2 twill."@en , "Scarf of woven silk and wool, Great Britain, ca. 1825-1845"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6033f36-8194-3f29-a763-df63577584c9/dimension/6> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6033f36-8194-3f29-a763-df63577584c9/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6033f36-8194-3f29-a763-df63577584c9/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6033f36-8194-3f29-a763-df63577584c9/dimension/5> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6033f36-8194-3f29-a763-df63577584c9/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d6033f36-8194-3f29-a763-df63577584c9/dimension/3> ;
